{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Collision analysis (paused pending coordination).\n\nThis BUG (c6bd-b10e-74f1-407f) and lemuroid-compliant-hoopoe (39a2-4832-e436-4850, in_progress, actively worked by a sibling agent) describe the SAME root cause and SAME fix, and hoopoe has declared file_impact on the IDENTICAL files.\n\nConfirmed mechanism (matches the recorded RCA): resolve_ref() in src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py (~L262-266) calls fetch_origin() with no target ref before rev_parse, which becomes 'git fetch --quiet --no-filter origin' in git_fetch.fetch_origin (~L256-283). On a checkout whose remote.origin.fetch maps every head, git transfers all origin heads (incl. the large tickets branch) even when only a locally-present code SHA is needed -> 300s timeout, zero model calls.\n\nFix location is a single shared seam (resolve_ref/fetch_origin) that hoopoe already owns via declared file_impact:\n- src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py\n- src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py\n- new test tests/unit/test_snapshot_targeted_fetch.py\n\nConfirmed the general fetch here is ONLY for ref freshness/resolution: blob acquisition for the selected tree is handled separately by _ensure_blobs_present() (targeted 'git fetch --no-filter --refetch <sha>'), so skipping the general fetch for a present full SHA preserves complete blob materialization. Proposed minimal fix: in resolve_ref, when ref is a full 40-hex SHA that rev_parse resolves locally, return it WITHOUT any general fetch; moving branches/tags still fetch; an absent SHA still uses the existing targeted-fetch fallback.\n\nBecause hoopoe is actively editing the same two functions, implementing here independently would collide on the same lines and duplicate the work. I have messaged the hoopoe agent to coordinate ownership (absorb fossa as duplicate, vs. I take a non-overlapping slice: the present-full-SHA regression test + docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md fetch-scope update layered on hoopoe's change). Holding all code edits until hoopoe replies."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787551954445734001,"uuid":"e3cf1a27-4756-4a47-be1c-4bb5f8871495"}